{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"FOUR_TICKET_PROSE_AUDIT_RECEIPT:d6669496:autositic-dizzy-necessary-unable\n\nFour-ticket prose-plan audit receipt (2026-09-05)\n\nFrozen source basis and audit-worktree HEAD: d6669496cae441fc8381b5ee6de21a3993defd84. Fresh fetch left origin/main at 4c9940348148fb255b17ddf1cb124701ad4565d7; all 72 scoped blobs are byte-identical across that range, and the worktree remained clean.\n\nAudited scope: 437 editable prose blocks (266 leading docstrings + 171 maximal full-line comment regions), 53,225 base words. Fifty-two concise/policy-load-bearing blocks remain excluded; 922 other prose blocks, 86 directive lines, one shebang, all inline prose, runtime strings, and executable AST are protected. Legacy ranges were remapped by owner/code identity, with occurrence-qualified duplicate anchors.\n\nExact persisted payloads:\n- autositic-relaxative-nurseshark (0165-f364-7afd-4d97): 96 blocks; description 7,308 chars / dedc7c67af658d25b18232317b67ff8ca18f8ffcac7e709b79d936e53f583b31; impacts 42d2c520cd55fdda907d5ba6d974c732f208e611720252207f9f384bb071713a; commands 7fa0f97314aaaee5a2b38e34d77802be899cbd4307bf8390e84efb08abe37889.\n- dizzy-muscovite-drever (063d-3adf-d5a4-4fa4): 106 blocks; description 7,477 chars / 4dbf1630321560210e08d4ccc772a5f7a282df0cdbc67da3a5693e47f0bb13e4; impacts e7ab07ec0324e5d35b11a447e89323be89b19ed6af1016cdd790c06c94fa9572; commands 613b9976ffbd2c363c3a91287fac5dd70e78a3a440063994387af4b793b2e1ed.\n- necessary-subtle-cooter (0d9f-df62-f5ad-4bb8): 111 blocks; description 7,241 chars / 3d6581a1edfc7568c2342ba6c4f2affcda713e168d4ba466fbcf7786201adfad; impacts 03fbf834e8f2f74bceae56100ee5e5b82169e7d350dc4ba1fb21de31da8d4e63; commands a31faa5eb79dbe9a961db5dfb834c5219e2e9eb7578ee139554fff1b389d4d77.\n- unable-wingless-bustard (143f-b548-c740-4da7): 124 blocks; description 7,842 chars / 94088024f40116614107ffdafbaef44907be55d124a1b4dcd31f0ca0e6fc78c3; impacts 1ab75295e72ab0d8b2a0c0a03aef2abb1c57d408ad64735b781e324d42719df0; commands 21e9f987702bd6ca724f28d95b5f6607866b3742cb34dcb0594a6eff34f3db80.\n\nEach ticket has exactly 18 ordered file-impact rows and seven DD rows in this order: immutable-prose-only, exact-leaf-paths, focused-tests, scoped-ruff, comment-hygiene, diff-integrity, repository-gates. The semantic oracle parses with type comments, strips only allowlisted leading docstrings, normalizes only TypeIgnore.lineno, compares HEAD^ to HEAD, preserves protected prose/directives/shebang attachment and runtime AST, requires every target shorter, and confines zero-context hunks to resolved spans/adjacent blanks. Consumer constraints include get_rotation.json, nested FastMCP tool docstrings, all explain-criterion guide names, Pydantic/FastMCP contracts, and the public package docstring.\n\nStatic validation only: all 28 commands passed `rtk proxy zsh -n -c`; all eight Python -c bodies passed shlex splitting and ast.parse. No persisted command, test, Ruff check, hygiene check, or make verify was executed.\n\nDelivery/readback: the first three tickets' nine MCP writes returned result=ok, push_status.state=ok, and null warnings. Unable's MCP edit was reconciled to the same clean acknowledgment; its remaining writes used the documented repo-venv CLI fallback after an MCP lock failure (181s, live pid=1) and two 300s MCP show timeouts. That fallback and exact field-normalized readbacks are recorded on skaldic-carbon-copperhead. Final fallback projections matched every description byte, ordered impact row, and normalized command triple. All four remain open, unassigned, under d6eb-1c6c-88c3-48f6, in planning, with the fresh preflight showing empty attestations.\n\nNo plan review, claim, source edit, implementation test/gate, transition, commit, or code push was performed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788639011420062001,"uuid":"a9a694fb-7205-4387-ba6e-8d815ef86ac7"}